# CommonMapsPlugin

A UE5 editor plugin for quickly switching between frequently used maps in your project.
Inspired by the Common Maps feature from Epic Games' Lyra Starter Game.

## Features

- **Toolbar dropdown** — One-click access to bookmarked maps grouped by category
- **Content Browser integration** — Right-click any Level asset to add it to a category
- **Editor Preferences panel** — Full CRUD via Edit → Editor Preferences → Plugins → Common Maps
- **Stale map detection** — Missing assets shown with ⚠ and disabled in the dropdown
- **Duplicate prevention** — Adding an existing map shows a notification instead of silently failing
- **Per-developer config** — Stored in EditorPerProjectUserSettings.ini, not source controlled

## Planned

- Right-click remove from category (v0.5)
- Recent maps auto-section in toolbar (v0.6)
- Custom drag-and-drop Editor Preferences panel (v0.7)

## Engine Version

UE 5.7+

## Installation

1. Copy `CommonMapsPlugin/` into your project's `Plugins/` directory
2. Regenerate project files
3. Enable via Edit → Plugins → Editor → Common Maps
4. Restart the editor

## Usage

**Adding a map**
Right-click any Level asset in the Content Browser → Add to Common Maps → pick a category

**Opening a map**
Click the Common Maps button in the toolbar → pick a map

**Managing categories**
Edit → Editor Preferences → Plugins → Common Maps

## Development Phases

| Tag | What was built |
|-----|----------------|
| `v0.1-foundation` | Module skeleton, settings class, Editor Preferences panel |
| `v0.2-toolbar` | Toolbar dropdown with map switching |
| `v0.3-context-menu` | Content Browser right-click to add maps |
| `v0.4-polish` | Stale detection, notifications, meta specifiers, persistence fix |

## Troubleshooting

**Maps not persisting after editor restart**
Ensure the plugin is enabled and the ini section exists at:
`Saved/Config/WindowsEditor/EditorPerProjectUserSettings.ini`
Look for `[/Script/CommonMaps.CommonMapSettings]`

**"Add to Common Maps" not appearing on right-click**
Only appears on Level assets (UWorld). Will not show on Blueprints, textures, etc.

**Toolbar button missing**
Check Output Log for `CommonMaps: StartupModule` — if absent the plugin didn't load.
Verify `PostEngineInit` loading phase in `.uplugin`.

